leo_lynx: Hey CS/eng 00 We're onboarding Lynx mobile SDK v1.2.0. During background syncs we're seeing intermittent 429s from /v1/preflight and occasional 502s from a regional edge. Syncs spike when app resumes and tries to refresh tokens + sync queued messages. Any mitigation suggestions?

nina_cs: Hi @leo_lynx 00 welcome! Can you share one full response body and an example x-request-id from a 429 and a 502? Also curious whether you're using ephemeral tokens or long-lived keys for mobile.

leo_lynx: 429 body: {"error":"rate_limited","retry_after":"30"} x-request-id: req_xL9. 502 body: upstream error from edge-lon-2. We're using ephemeral tokens rotated every 10m, and we kick a refresh during resume with no cap.

ethan_eng: Thanks. Two things likely happen: (1) token refresh fanout from many devices resuming simultaneously, (2) edge LB returning 502 under transient overload and then upstream 429s from preflight if requests queue.

leo_lynx: We do have a background sync that tries to flush queue on resume. On iOS it can fire for many suspended sessions when user opens app after updates.

nina_cs: Quick client mitigations: add random jitter to resume refreshes (0-15s), limit concurrent preflight calls to N (we suggest 3), and persist a short-lived token cache so multiple tabs/devices reuse a token when possible. Also implement retry with full jitter and cap max retries.

ethan_eng: Server-side: we can enable preflight coalescing for your org (merges similar preflight requests into one backend call) and bump your onboarding burst quota for the migration window. Need org id and expected parallel resume count.

leo_lynx: org_lynxA. Expect ~400 devices over ~2m during a staged rollout tomorrow. We'll try client caps but timeline is tight.

ops-bot: ops-bot: scheduled rollout detected for lynx-mobile v1.2.0 @ 2025-01-08T09:10:12Z

mobile-deploy-bot: mobile-deploy-bot: canary build passed.

ethan_eng: Filed CS-4987 to request temporary onboarding bump and preflight coalescing toggle for org_lynxA. Requested 2000 r/min for 6h and coalescing enabled at edge-lon-2. Adding edge team to watch for 502 patterns.

nina_cs: For immediate relief, implement client-side semaphore to limit background sync concurrency. Example pseudo: 

```
const sem = new Semaphore(3);
async function onResume() {
  await sem.acquire();
  try {
    await refreshEphemeral();
    await flushQueue();
  } finally { sem.release(); }
}
```

Also add randomized delay before first refresh.

leo_lynx: Nice, we'll add semaphore + jitter and short-lived local token cache (10s) so concurrent resume uses same token. We'll run canary in EU region first.

ethan_eng: One more note: if you see Retry-After 30s from preflight, backoff aggressively and surface a logistic message to users explaining sync will resume shortly. That reduces reattempts and user retries.

nina_cs: I've included support on-call for the canary window. We'll monitor preflight 429 counts and edge 502s and escalate if the quota change doesn't clear it.

leo_lynx: Great, canary running in eu-west-1 now. I'll post results in ~30m. Appreciate the help!
